{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_iopsewzaa4y36kp6mbmlsz4htjfcg3mubbyiffmwrflxegbrmp3a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_011W9rPsVxSh8dGt6R3whr7f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-tpHMdy/translated_rust/CONFIGS.md","content":"# CONFIGS.md — Phase A: configuration-surface table\n\n## Build-time configurations\n\n`Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]` table** and `src/` contains **no\n`#[cfg(feature = ...)]`** (`grep -rn feature src/` -> no matches).\n`c_src/CMakeLists.txt` has no `option()`, no `target_compile_definitions`, and\nno `#ifdef` in `c_src/src/lib.c` or `c_src/include/lib.h`.\n\nTherefore the **complete** set of valid feature combinations is exactly one: the\nempty set. It is verified under both of the ways it can be spelled, plus both\nCargo profiles (`dev` and `release`, which differ here because\n`[profile.release] panic = \"abort\"`):\n\n| # | build configuration | command |\n|---|---------------------|---------|\n| B1 | default (= no features) | `cargo test` |\n| B2 | explicit no-default-features | `cargo test --no-default-features` |\n| B3 | all-features (= no features) | `cargo test --all-features` |\n| B4 | release (`panic = \"abort\"`) | `cargo test --release` |\n| B5 | release + no-default-features | `cargo test --release --no-default-features` |\n\n## Runtime configuration axes\n\n`ima_parse(struct ima_info *info, const void *data)` is the only public entry\npoint (`c_src/include/lib.h`), and it takes **no** flags, modes, or length. All\nconfiguration is therefore the *shape and content of the `data` byte stream*.\nThe axes below are the ones the C actually branches on, taken from its `if` /\n`else if` / `for(;;)` structure:\n\n* **A1 — `header->type`** (bytes 0..4): `'caff'` vs. anything else -> `-1`.\n* **A2 — `header->version`** (BE u16 at 4..6): `1` vs. anything else -> `-2`.\n* **A3 — `header->flags`** (bytes 6..8): never read; must be inert.\n* **A4 — chunk list shape**: which of `desc` / `pakt` / `data` appear, in what\n  order, how many times, and how many unknown chunks are interleaved.\n  `desc` and `pakt` are *latched* (last one before `data` wins) and only `data`\n  terminates the loop.\n* **A5 — `chunk->size`** (BE s64 at chunk+8): drives the walk stride\n  (`chunk += 16 + size`) and, for the `data` chunk, becomes `info->size`.\n  Sign, zero, and overflow all matter.\n* **A6 — chunk `type` padding** (bytes chunk+4..chunk+8): the 4 bytes of C\n  struct tail padding; never read; must be inert.\n* **A7 — `desc->format_id`** (chunk+16+8): `'ima4'` vs. anything else -> `-3`.\n* **A8 — `desc->sample_rate`** (chunk+16+0): 8 raw bytes read as a *native*\n  `double`, then `double`->`u64` value-converted, byte-swapped, and bit-cast.\n  The classes the x86-64 lowering distinguishes are the sub-axes below.\n* **A9 — `desc->channels_per_frame`** (chunk+16+24): copied out via `bswap32`.\n* **A10 — `pakt->frame_count`** (chunk+16+8): copied out via `bswap64`.\n* **A11 — ignored `desc`/`pakt` fields**: `format_flags`, `bytes_per_packet`,\n  `frames_per_packet`, `bits_per_channel`, `packet_count`, `priming_frames`,\n  `remainder_frames`, and `caf_data::edit_count`; all must be inert.\n* **A12 — buffer base alignment**: the C casts raw pointers to structs needing\n  8-byte alignment; the Rust uses `read_unaligned`. Offsets 0..8 of the buffer\n  base must all behave identically.\n\n`info` output is compared as all **40 raw bytes** of `struct ima_info` (including\nthe 4 tail padding bytes after `channel_count`, which neither side may write),\nwith `blocks` compared as an absolute pointer — both libraries are handed the\n*same* buffer, so the pointer value itself must match exactly.\n\n## Configuration rows\n\nEvery row is driven with many randomized inputs from a fixed-seed SplitMix64\nPRNG (`tests/common/mod.rs`), not a single hand-picked value.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1 | `ima_parse` | A1 valid, A2 valid, `desc`+`pakt`+`data` in that order, all fields random, `size` random small non-negative | [x] |\n| 2 | `ima_parse` | A4: `pakt` before `desc` (reversed latch order) | [x] |\n| 3 | `ima_parse` | A4: `data` chunk first-and-only after a `desc`+`pakt`; zero unknown chunks | [x] |\n| 4 | `ima_parse` | A4: 1 unknown chunk interleaved between `desc` and `pakt` | [x] |\n| 5 | `ima_parse` | A4: many (8..32) unknown chunks with random types/sizes interleaved | [x] |\n| 6 | `ima_parse` | A4: duplicate `desc` chunks — the **last** before `data` must win | [x] |\n| 7 | `ima_parse` | A4: duplicate `pakt` chunks — the **last** before `data` must win | [x] |\n| 8 | `ima_parse` | A4: `desc`/`pakt` appearing *after* the `data` chunk (must be ignored — loop already broke) | [x] |\n| 9 | `ima_parse` | A5: `data` chunk `size` = 0 | [x] |\n| 10 | `ima_parse` | A5: `data` chunk `size` = random full-range `i64` (incl. negative), -> `info->size` | [x] |\n| 11 | `ima_parse` | A5: `data` chunk `size` = boundary set {0,1,-1,i64::MIN,i64::MAX,2^31,2^32,2^47,-2^31} | [x] |\n| 12 | `ima_parse` | A5: unknown chunk with `size` = 0 (stride exactly 16) | [x] |\n| 13 | `ima_parse` | A5: unknown chunk with negative `size` that walks backwards onto a valid `data` chunk | [x] |\n| 14 | `ima_parse` | A6: chunk tail-padding bytes randomized on every chunk (must be inert) | [x] |\n| 15 | `ima_parse` | A3: `header->flags` swept over random + boundary values (must be inert) | [x] |\n| 16 | `ima_parse` | A8: `sample_rate` = realistic big-endian `f64` (44100/48000/8000/96000) — the common real-world case, which reads as a tiny subnormal and truncates to 0 | [x] |\n| 17 | `ima_parse` | A8: `sample_rate` raw bytes = uniformly random 8 bytes (hits negative/NaN/Inf/huge -> the UB region) | [x] |\n| 18 | `ima_parse` | A8: `sample_rate` LE bit pattern chosen so the native `double` is in `[0, 2^63)` — the well-defined conversion range | [x] |\n| 19 | `ima_parse` | A8: `sample_rate` native `double` in `[2^63, 2^64)` — the `subsd`/`xor` branch | [x] |\n| 20 | `ima_parse` | A8: `sample_rate` native `double` `>= 2^64` and `= +Inf` — indefinite via the `subsd` branch | [x] |\n| 21 | `ima_parse` | A8: `sample_rate` native `double` negative (incl. `-0.0`, `-Inf`, small negatives, `< -2^63`) | [x] |\n| 22 | `ima_parse` | A8: `sample_rate` native `double` = quiet NaN, signalling NaN, and NaN with random payloads | [x] |\n| 23 | `ima_parse` | A8: `sample_rate` native `double` at exact conversion boundaries: `2^63-1024`, `2^63`, `2^63+2048`, `2^64-2048`, `2^64`, `-2^63`, `-2^63-2048`, `±f64::MIN_POSITIVE`, `±0.0`, subnormals | [x] |\n| 24 | `ima_parse` | A9: `channels_per_frame` = random u32 + boundaries {0,1,2,0x7fffffff,0x80000000,0xffffffff} | [x] |\n| 25 | `ima_parse` | A10: `frame_count` = random u64 + boundaries {0,1,-1,i64::MIN,i64::MAX,u64::MAX} | [x] |\n| 26 | `ima_parse` | A11: every ignored field set to random garbage (must be inert) | [x] |\n| 27 | `ima_parse` | A12: buffer base offset by 0..8 bytes within a larger allocation (misaligned `desc`/`pakt`/`chunk`) | [x] |\n| 28 | `ima_parse` | A7 valid + full random cross-product: random chunk-list shape x random `size` x random `sample_rate` bytes x random ignored fields, 20000 iterations | [x] |\n| 29 | `ima_parse` | `blocks` output pointer: asserted to equal `buf + (data chunk offset) + 20` for random chunk-list shapes | [x] |\n| 30 | `ima_parse` | A2: all 65536 `header->version` values swept (exactly one must yield != -2) | [x] |\n| 31 | `ima_parse` | A1: random 4-byte `header->type` values incl. every 1-byte mutation of `\"caff\"` | [x] |\n| 32 | `ima_parse` | A16/row-16: random 4-byte chunk types incl. every 1-byte mutation of `\"desc\"`/`\"pakt\"`/`\"data\"` | [x] |\n| 33 | `ima_parse` | `info` pre-filled with a poison pattern; all 40 bytes compared, incl. tail padding, on both success and every error return | [x] |\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3840,"cache_read_input_tokens":54925,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3840,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3786f768-af92-404b-a5c1-7f882bb95312","uuid":"015531d2-16e1-41ba-87a1-f08c1d4a8070","timestamp":"2026-08-19T13:06:14.070Z"}
