{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_bx25jo2yrdjvpfpy7ybfxa6535dfymrtp4ua6qvyz6ua6nphu3na","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four completion-gate criteria hold.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src` is a 131-line CAF (Core Audio Format) parser exporting exactly one symbol, `ima_parse`. Critically, its `struct caf_chunk { u32 type; s64 size; }` gets 4 bytes of x86-64 tail padding, so the C walks the stream with **16-byte** chunk headers (not the 12 bytes real CAF uses) and places `blocks` at `chunk+20`. I confirmed every offset and constant against `objdump -d` of the C `.so` rather than assuming — all recorded in `SYMBOLS.md`.\n\n## Results\n\n- **Phase A** — `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md` (20 rows), `CONFIGS.md` (34 rows + 5 build configs). No `[features]` exists in `Cargo.toml` and no `#cfg(feature)` in `src/`, so the feature cross-product is the single empty set; I verified it under all spellings plus both profiles, which turned out to matter a lot.\n- **Phase B** — 34/34 rows pass, driven through both `.so`s via `libloading`, comparing the return code and all **40 raw bytes** of `ima_info` (including tail padding, and `blocks` as an absolute pointer, since both get the same buffer).\n- **Phase C** — 20/20 rows pass, including 8 fault/hang rows run in re-exec'd child processes.\n- **Phase D** — `nm -D` diff is empty (`ima_parse` only) in every configuration.\n\n## Two real bugs found and fixed\n\n**1. Wrong signal on null/wild pointers** (rows 4–8 initially failed). The translation used `ptr::read_unaligned`, which is wrong for reproducing a C raw load in two independent ways: it forwards to `copy_nonoverlapping`, whose `debug_assertions`-only \"is not null\" precondition fires `panic_nounwind` → **SIGABRT** where C gives **SIGSEGV**; and with optimization on, a plain load from a provably-invalid pointer is UB that LLVM **deletes outright** — I measured the release build exiting 0 with no fault at all. Same problem on the `(*info).field = …` stores. Both now use `read_volatile`/`write_volatile` through an `align == 1` `#[repr(C, packed)]` wrapper: alignment is trivially satisfied (so misaligned bases still work), there's no null precondition, and volatile accesses can't be elided.\n\nThis is exactly the class of bug the dev/release split exposes — neither profile alone would have caught it.\n\n**2. My own test bugs, not the Rust's.** 7 Phase B failures were in my expected-value assertions (I double-applied the byte swap — the builder writes big-endian and the C's `btoh` undoes it). And my first `row20` segfaulted the test process because the walk only ever visits offsets ≡ 8 mod 16, so my planted stop chunk was missed. Worth flagging: `assert_same` never fired in either case, so C and Rust already agreed.\n\n## Notable verification depth\n\nThe riskiest line is `conv64.u = desc->sample_rate` — a **float→integer value conversion**, not a bit cast, which is UB for negative/NaN/Inf/≥2^64 inputs. The Rust emulates GCC's `comisd`/`jae`/`cvttsd2si`/`subsd`/`xor` lowering. I fuzzed it with 10⁶ inputs with measured branch coverage (371611 in-range / 191541 `subsd` / 311709 negative / 125139 NaN) and replayed the whole suite against C rebuilt at `-O0/-O1/-O2/-O3/-Os` — all pass.\n\nOne honest limitation: rows 10/12/13 assert \"both faulted\" rather than \"same signal\". These fault on wild addresses from unchecked pointer arithmetic, and on x86-64 a **non-canonical** address raises a GP fault (SIGBUS) while canonical-but-unmapped raises SIGSEGV. `-O0/-O2/-O3/-Os` give SIGSEGV; `-O1` gives SIGBUS for `size == i64::MAX`. That's a property of the address, not the library, so I pinned the loop *logic* separately with an in-process byte-exact test over walks of 1…65535 unknown chunks. The null-pointer rows (4–8) have exact canonical addresses and do assert signal equality.\n\n`c_src/` is unmodified (checksums verified); `Cargo.toml` gained only `libloading` under `[dev-dependencies]`. `cargo clippy --all-targets` is clean. Re-run everything with `./run_all_configs.sh`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1317,"cache_read_input_tokens":211193,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1317,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3786f768-af92-404b-a5c1-7f882bb95312","uuid":"a8dfb6f6-0ed7-4589-a1f9-6cabfd696810","timestamp":"2026-08-19T13:32:25.001Z"}
